==Strategy==
The general idea here is to bring many meatshields and fill the remaining slots with [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] and [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critters]]. Stall the Metal One Horn and the Metal Doges for money. When you hit the base, lure the Sir Metal Seal to your base, then spam everything, possibly with a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]]. By this point, you should also own [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]], who should be able to deal hefty damage to the Sir Metal Seals and Super Metal Hippoes.

This is one of the stages where [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Banner Cat/Mochi Cat]] can really shine as his [[Weaken|weaken]] will help you keep them in control and his high weaken chance and short recharge time can make them weaken the enemies forever. A stack of [[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Bad-Luck Ebisu]] can also work in the first 3 crowns, provided you manage to stack him, as his many crowd control effects can help push back the enemies. Bring [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal cats]] and critical hitters as well, as you will need them (however, [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]] isn't very useful here due to the high amount of peons in the way).

[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] and [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]] might not be a good choice as a critical hitter in this stage. Because of Catornado's Area Attack and E. Kubilan's [[Wave Attack]]s, they have a tendency to take out the Metal Doges too early and have the Super Metal Hippoes stack with the Sir Metal Seals, which can be extremely dangerous unless you have the units to take them out quickly.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any Uber with a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and/or can do [[Critical Hit]]s with a decent chance, will be good here. Listed below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Marauder Cat]]: Just like most other stages full of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, Marauder Cat make this stage a joke as long as he is in his Evolved Form or higher.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: An even better option, can destroy most if not all of the [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies in this stage with his powerful, [[Long Distance]] strikes.
*[[Graveflower Verbena (Uber Rare Cat)|Graveflower Verbena]]: Another critical-hitting Uber, her [[Multi-Hit|Multi-Hits]] increase her chance of doing a Critical Hit on the Metal enemies here.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]]: Great [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] for all the [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies here and has a chance to do a [[Critical Hit]].
*[[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Wrathful Poseidon]]: Freezes the metals in their tracks, granting great respite for your remaining anti-metals.
*[[Mech Patrol Axel (Uber Rare Cat)|Steel Sergeant Axel]]: With the metal killer ability on both his main attack and conjure, he can do considerable damage, while also staying at a safe range. His freeze ability can also help greatly, giving your critical hitters more time to kill the metals.

